# Lost and Found Site - Frontend Development Rules

## Component Organization
- **Never use "use client" in a page component**. If client-side functionality is needed, create a `pageClient.tsx` file in the same folder as the page.
- Group components used in each page similar to how app routes work (folder-based organization).

## Styling & UI Components
- We are using **shadcn** and will depend on it heavily.
- If custom styling is needed, **edit the shadcn components directly** rather than creating separate styled components.
- Use a **fancy scrollbar throughout** - never use the browser default scrollbar.

## TypeScript & Code Quality
- **Always run `pnpm tsc --noEmit`** to check for TypeScript errors before finalizing code changes.

## Data Structure
- When building the frontend, use **real data structures** - meaning how the data will actually look after backend integration. Don't use placeholder or mock data structures that won't match the final API.

## Library Usage
- When asked for a solution to something, **always check if a React library handles it already** instead of building from scratch. Prefer existing, well-maintained libraries over custom implementations.

